# Documentation and the GitHub Pages site are published to the repo and to
# nikolareljin.github.io/leak-lock — they are not part of the runtime, and the
# site's screenshots alone are ~192K of dead weight in the .vsix. README.md and
# CHANGELOG.md stay, since the Marketplace renders them; vsce rewrites the
# README's relative docs/ links to absolute repository URLs, so they keep
# working from the listing.
docs/**

# CI, release and Dependabot configuration — build-time only.
.github/**
.githooks/**

# Generated by tools/release-notes.js during publishing, and generated *before*
# packaging, so it is present exactly when the .vsix is built. .gitignore keeps
# it out of the repository but vsce does not read .gitignore once a .vscodeignore
# exists, so without this line the release notes ship inside the extension.
.release-notes.md

# Screenshot tooling — development only.
tools/**

# Contributor and scratch notes, not shipped to users.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# Local agent/tooling state. These are gitignored, but .vscodeignore is a
# separate mechanism: vsce does not read .gitignore when a .vscodeignore file
# exists, so a working copy that has them ships them. `publish.sh` runs
# `vsce package` locally, which is one command away from putting session notes
# and local settings on the Marketplace. Published 0.7.5 escaped this only
# because it was released from a clean CI checkout.
.remember/**
.claude/**
.cursor/**
.aider*
.DS_Store

# credential-lens is bundled, not runtime-installed: 41 KB, zero dependencies,
# and it runs in-process. Removing these two lines produces an extension that
# loads cleanly and throws the first time a user opens a credential report.
!node_modules/@nikolareljin/**
!node_modules/@nikolareljin/credential-lens/**
